MobileGlues: every texture it makes is checked, and one it can't make is logged in full.

A level the driver can't make was silent: MobileGlues' own error logging is on in debug builds only, and its
glTexStorage2D read the driver's error away, so the game never learned either. On a Pixel 10's PowerVR three of the
game's atlases were never made: their 28,000 uploads failed, and saving the fast start cache read one as 0 bytes and
stopped the game (Pocket Foundry #65), with no line saying why. Now each glTexImage2D, glTexStorage2D and ASTC level
is checked: one that fails is logged with its texture, size, levels, the format asked and the one made, the driver's
error and how much was made before it, and the error goes back to the game; big ones made are logged too. A failing
upload says how the driver has its level, its first three per texture in full, then a count every 1,000.

